# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
#
# RDR-5, RDR-6 and RDR-8: page a long entry with `NEXT`, step back with
# Backspace, and leave by the far end. Since M5-E4d (#305) a page is a
# full screen, the same box the `Notes` listing is drawn in, so the
# give-back is the whole screen and not the roster's cells.
#
# **The keys are the `Notes` path since #346**, because there is no other:
# F1 opened a number prompt and both are gone. The frame ranges below
# were measured against the F1 script and have not been measured against
# this one - this leg is owed its re-drive with the rest (#293), and the
# keys are corrected here so that what it asks for is the reader that
# exists.
# A single leg, and it has to be one: the page covers the screen, so a
# rect that allowed it would check nothing, and the composer that puts
# the screen back resets the command bar's highlight, so the frames after
# Escape differ from a seam-off run on the bar row however exact the
# give-back is (#234).

about paging a long entry full-screen, and giving the screen back exactly
kind single
program START.EXE
store tests/visual/reader-store.txt
both code-wheel

# The code-wheel bypass is gated on the wheel itself (#115), pinned by
# digest because a document never enters this tree.
document 0db301aeac4d2ec1e63b409ca6d3c9d39c63381d6712ff2ce7edc0528c6586fd
seam journal
until 300000000
every 25

# A screen this seam draws is painted over successive arrivals, a few
# rows at a time, by the program's own drawing routines: about 230
# frames for a twenty-row page and about 130 for a ten-row listing,
# measured by hand (#305). A range starting sooner would measure the
# paint.
key A@7601
key Return@7651
key L@8951
key A@9201

# `Notes` opens the log, and Return opens the row the cursor is on, which
# is the long entry the store puts first.
key N@10600
key Return@10800

# Forward, back, forward, and then out through the far end: the entry is two
# pages at thirty-eight columns by twenty rows.
key N@11600
key Backspace@12400
key N@13200

# The way out, twice: `EXIT` off the page's own bar returns to the listing
# it was opened from (#305), and `EXIT` off the listing's composes the
# screen back.
key E@14000
key E@14800

rect bar 0,190,319,199

# Each page, holding still with nothing pressed.
same 11100-11575
same 11900-12375
same 12700-13175
same 13500-13975

# And the screen before the reader took it, back again after it: every pixel
# except the bar row, which was not-log-giveback.leg's finding - the
# give-back left the program's own bar highlight parked on the `Notes`
# group this seam had spliced on. Fixed since #330; the exception stays
# until this leg is re-driven on the shorter boot (#293), and rdr-bar.leg
# asserts the same give-back with nothing excepted.
equal 10600 15200 bar
